DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       These  functions calculate the complex arc sine of _z.  If _y _= _c_a_s_i_n_(_z_),
       then _z _= _c_s_i_n_(_y_).  The real  part  of  _y  is  chosen  in  the  interval
       [-pi/2,pi/2].

       One has:

           casin(z) = -i clog(iz + csqrt(1 - z * z))

